<title>VIETNAM: Petrovietnam Jan-Aug crude exports 5.5 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>Petrovietnam Jan-Aug crude exports 5.5 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>HANOI 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Petrovietnam, Vietnam's state-owned oil and gas company, exported 5.5 million tonnes of crude oil in the first eight months of this year, the official Vietnam News Agency (VNA) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>VNA gave no comparative data for the same period of 1995, but said the figure was equivalent to the total volume exported for the whole of 1992.</p>
<p>Since 1987, Petrovietnam has exported 41 million tonnes of crude.</p>
<p>VNA said the oil exported in January-August, which was pumped from the Bach Ho (White Tiger) and Dai Hung (Big Bear) offshore oilfields, earned the company more than $800 million.</p>
</text>
